WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.370
These two photographs show the same man:
Alexander Upshaw,

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.430
a Crow man educated
at the Carlisle Indian School,

3
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.090
who worked as an interpreter.

4
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:14.590
On the right is Frank Rinehart's 1898 portrait
of Upshaw in a suit and tie.

5
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.220
On the left is Curtis's
1905 photograph of him

6
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.230
in a feathered headdress
and long bead necklaces, posed outdoors.

7
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.490
Upshaw even worked for Curtis
as an interpreter and assistant.

8
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.850
In Curtis's version, the modern,
educated man disappears.
